  "report_discrepancies": [],
  "notes": "Governmental funds cash basis; business-type funds accrual. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p5); business-type from the proprietary funds statement Totals column (p7): receipts = operating revenues + interest income, disbursements = operating expenses + debt issuance costs + interest expense (= Statement of Activities business-type expenses 3,139,187, p3). No restatement or prior period adjustment is printed for FY2023 (business-type beginning 5,537,874 and governmental fund balance 983,136 as printed). Governmental cash is printed only as separate lines (cash in bank, CDs, county treasurer, restricted), no single cash total, so beginning/ending cash are left null. Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), lines tagged by column. Detail: General Fund from its combining schedule (pp11-12), one line per sub-fund column (Eliminations column of transfers 537,170 not recorded; department transfers net to the Total 738,600); the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (p8) is not recorded (same totals, less detailed). Streets and Alley and Sales Tax Funds from their budget schedules (pp9-10). Utility funds have no supplementary schedules, so no business-type detail (as FY2024; proprietary statement fund-column lines removed since other funds have their own schedules). Fire column spending is printed on the Public Works row. Read pages 1-13 of 13."
}
